{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Access Control - Network Zones - Okta Network Zone Deactivated",
	"Description": "An Okta network zone was deactivated. Zones are what policies use to say \"only from the office\" or \"never from this country\", so deactivating one silently widens every policy that referenced it.\n\nEvent type: zone.deactivate\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_okta_attempt_to_deactivate_okta_network_zone/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
